\section*{Prerequisite Diagnostic}
Complete without a calculator unless your course normally permits one.

\begin{enumerate}
\item Expand \((x+h)^2\).
\item Factor \(x^2-9\).
\item Simplify \((x^2-4)/(x-2)\) for \(x\ne2\).
\item Rewrite \(1/x^3\) with a negative exponent.
\item Rewrite \(\sqrt[3]{x^2}\) with a rational exponent.
\item Simplify \(\frac{1/(x+h)-1/x}{h}\).
\item Solve \(3x^2-12x+9=0\).
\item State the slope formula through \((x_1,y_1)\) and \((x_2,y_2)\).
\item Write the point-slope equation for slope \(4\) through \((2,-1)\).
\item Evaluate \(\lim_{h\to0}[(2+h)^2-4]/h\).
\item State \(\lim_{u\to0}\sin u/u\).
\item For \(f(x)=x^2\), calculate \(f(a+h)-f(a)\).
\end{enumerate}

\begin{bgreveal}
Answers: \(x^2+2xh+h^2\); \((x-3)(x+3)\); \(x+2\); \(x^{-3}\); \(x^{2/3}\); \(-1/[x(x+h)]\); \(x=1,3\); \((y_2-y_1)/(x_2-x_1)\); \(y+1=4(x-2)\); \(4\); \(1\); \(2ah+h^2\).
\end{bgreveal}

\begin{bgmethod}[title={How to use the result}]
Missing zero to two items: begin the unit. Missing three to five: review the attached algebra topics while starting the first conceptual lessons. Missing six or more: repair factoring, exponents, rational expressions, and limits first. This is not gatekeeping; it is the shortest route through the material.
\end{bgmethod}
