\section{Foundation Review}
\begin{bgsummary}
\begin{itemize}
\item \(f'(a)\) is the limit of average rates over shrinking nonzero intervals.
\item It is both an instantaneous rate and a tangent slope.
\item The derivative function maps each input to its tangent slope.
\item Derivative units are output units per input unit.
\item Differentiability implies continuity, but continuity does not guarantee differentiability.
\end{itemize}
\end{bgsummary}

