\section{Review}
\begin{bgsummary}
\begin{itemize}
\item Implicit differentiation treats \(y\) as a function of \(x\), so every derivative of a \(y\)-expression includes \(y'\).
\item Inverse-function slopes are reciprocal at corresponding points.
\item Inverse trig derivatives follow from implicit differentiation and identities.
\item Logarithmic differentiation converts products to sums, quotients to differences, and powers to coefficients.
\end{itemize}
\end{bgsummary}

